10
00:49:07,826 --> 00:49:13,826
The Meg is a 2018 science fiction action film directed by Jon Turteltaub from a screenplay by Dean Georgaris, Jon
Hoeber, and Erich Hoeber, loosely based on the 1997 novel Meg: A Novel of Deep Terror by Steve Alten.

11
00:54:02,608 --> 00:54:08,608
The film stars Jason Statham, Li Bingbing, Rainn Wilson,
Ruby Rose, Winston Chao, and Cliff Curtis.

12
00:58:57,391 --> 00:59:03,391
In the plot, a group of scientists encounters a 75-foot-long (23 m) megalodon
while on a rescue mission on the floor of the Pacific Ocean.

13
01:03:52,173 --> 01:03:58,173
Walt Disney Studios originally purchased the film rights to the novel in
the 1990s, but the film spent years in development hell.

14
01:08:46,956 --> 01:08:52,956
The rights eventually landed at Warner Bros.

15
01:13:41,739 --> 01:13:47,739
Pictures, and the film was green-lit in 2013.

16
01:18:36,521 --> 01:18:42,521
Turteltaub and much of the cast joined by September 2014.

17
01:23:31,304 --> 01:23:37,304
Principal photography began in October 2016 and lasted until
January 2017, occurring in New Zealand and China.

18
01:28:26,086 --> 01:28:32,086
The Meg was released in the United States on August 10, 2018.

19
01:33:20,869 --> 01:33:26,869
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $529 million
worldwide against a production budget of $130–178 million.

20
01:38:15,652 --> 01:38:21,652
A sequel, Meg 2: The Trench, was released in 2023, with Georgaris and the Hoebers returning as
writers and Statham, Curtis, Sophia Cai and Page Kennedy reprising their roles.

21
01:43:10,434 --> 01:43:16,434
The film explores themes of beach, based on novel or
book, deep sea, underwater, shark.

22
01:48:05,217 --> 01:48:11,217
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
